---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import DecodingPlayground from '../components/widgets/DecodingPlayground.svelte';
import { chapters } from '../data/chapters';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base title="Home">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>All You Need to Know About dLLMs</h1>
    <p class="tag">
      An interactive tutorial on diffusion language models: what they are, how
      they decode, why they exist, and when to use one. Every number is cited,
      and every animation is a real model decoding.
    </p>
    <p class="asof">As of July 2026</p>
  </section>

  <blockquote class="anchor">
    Generative sequence modelling is <strong>repeatedly predicting clean tokens
    from a corrupted context</strong>. Autoregression and diffusion differ only
    in the corruption process and the decoding order. Nine chapters unpack that
    sentence.
  </blockquote>

  <DecodingPlayground client:visible autoplay={true} compact={true} />

  <h2>Chapters</h2>
  <ul class="cards">
    {chapters.map((c) => (
      <li class="card">
        <a href={`${base}/${c.slug}/`}>
          <span class="n">CHAPTER {c.n}</span>
          <h3>{c.title}</h3>
          <p>{c.hook}</p>
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2>What this is, and is not</h2>
  <p>
    This site is the interactive companion to a 90-page tutorial,
    <em>The Past and Present of Text Diffusion Models</em>, and curates its
    dLLM story: the anchor idea, the masked objective, decoding, the
    block dial, the family taxonomy, post-training, serving, and safety. The
    heavy derivations (DDPM ELBO, score entropy, discrete flow matching's
    velocity algebra) stay in the PDF, where they are done in full. The small
    model whose decodes power the widgets here is 1.85M parameters, trained on
    Shakespeare in minutes; its role is to make mechanisms observable, not to
    demonstrate capability.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: 2.4rem;
    background: linear-gradient(100deg, var(--hero-a), var(--hero-b) 55%, var(--hero-c));
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
    color: transparent;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .tag { font-size: 1.08rem; color: var(--gray); max-width: 38rem; }
  .anchor {
    margin: 1.8rem 0;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--amber);
    padding: 0.5rem 1.1rem;
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    background: #fdf9f1;
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
  }
</style>
